WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en
Style:
::cue(c.colorCCCCCC) { color: rgb(204,204,204);
 }
::cue(c.cyan) { color: cyan; }
::cue(c.yellow) { color: yellow; }
##

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.740 line:85%
This is gonna be in a simulator.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.106 line:91%
I'm just gonna set that
expectation at the start.

00:00:04.106 --> 00:00:06.553 position:56% line:91%
If you clicked on this thinking that
someone had miraculously

00:00:06.553 --> 00:00:09.315 line:91%
given an idiot
an actual jumbo jet to land...

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.485 line:85%
No, this is a simulator.

00:00:11.485 --> 00:00:13.799 line:91%
But this is Petter from
Mentour Pilot,

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.550 position:58% line:91%
who is a qualified pilot and
qualified training instructor, right?

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.956 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yes, correct.</c>

00:00:18.956 --> 00:00:21.838 line:91%
<c.yellow>I work with instructing new pilots
and examining new pilots</c>

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:24.484 line:91%
<c.yellow>before they're allowed to
actually fly the real aircraft,</c>

00:00:24.484 --> 00:00:26.820 line:91%
<c.yellow>and after they're allowed
to fly the real aircraft as well.</c>

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.196 position:56% line:91%
And so over on your channel,
you are gonna be doing the breakdown

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:31.798 line:91%
of everything you are
about to tell me

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.605 line:91%
from your air traffic control
centre through there.

00:00:34.605 --> 00:00:35.745 line:85%
<c.yellow>Exactly. That's the idea.</c>

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:37.456 line:91%
Yeah, you're not gonna be
in there with me.

00:00:37.456 --> 00:00:41.808 line:91%
I'm gonna be on my own
in the disaster movie scenario

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.407 line:91%
where I am the only one
left conscious on the plane.

00:00:45.407 --> 00:00:47.816 line:91%
And... I dunno, what do you
think my odds are?

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:49.650 line:85%
<c.yellow>I'd say they're pretty good.</c>

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.309 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'd say in the
high 20 percentile, yeah.</c>

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.150 line:85%
Right, okay.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.489 line:91%
<c.yellow>But in order for me to know that,
really, I need to know:</c>

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.440 line:91%
<c.yellow>Do you have any previous
experience at all?</c>

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.381 line:85%
I've been in one flight simulator

00:01:00.381 --> 00:01:02.640 line:91%
for a Comic Relief video
many, many years ago.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.940 line:91%
But they just put us on
the easiest version.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.060 line:91%
We were already coming in
to land, and it was just:

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.706 line:91%
keep the controls straight,
you'll be fine.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.270 line:85%
This is a motion based simulator.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.850 line:91%
It's gonna move.
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.365 line:91%
Which we have been given for free
for the whole day

00:01:16.365 --> 00:01:19.161 line:91%
in exchange for me saying that
this is the brand new

00:01:19.161 --> 00:01:21.313 line:91%
Airline Flight Academy
Simulator Centre in Dublin,

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:24.630 position:67% line:91%
with six state of the art flight simulators
that provides top class training services,

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.460 position:58% line:91%
including B737 and A320 type ratings
and industry leading APS MCC courses.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.215 line:85%
<i>(inhale)</i><00:01:30.369><c> There we go.</c>

00:01:31.215 --> 00:01:32.660 line:85%
<c.yellow>Excellent. Well done.</c>

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.164 line:91%
Alright.
Next time I see you,

00:01:35.164 --> 00:01:37.020 line:85%
I will have either landed or...

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.399 line:85%
...landed the hard way.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:40.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>Correct. And I'm gonna
go this way.</c>

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.927 line:85%
Thank you! <i>(wheezes)</i>

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:47.579 line:76%
Okay, I'm in position.
Seatbelt on.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:50.000 line:7%
I guess this is the first cheat,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.559 position:56% line:8%
which is that I would never have got
through that cockpit door, right?

00:01:52.559 --> 00:01:53.534 line:85%
<c.yellow>Absolutely.</c>

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:56.975 line:91%
<c.yellow>So we have to do this
as a theoretical scenario</c>

00:01:56.975 --> 00:02:00.869 line:91%
<c.yellow>where you have gotten access
to the cockpit in some fashion.</c>

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.813 line:91%
<c.yellow>But in reality,
in an emergency like this,</c>

00:02:03.813 --> 00:02:06.904 line:91%
<c.yellow>a passenger would never get access
through the closed cockpit door.</c>

00:02:07.454 --> 00:02:12.091 position:56% line:91%
And would never be able to magically
conjure up an air traffic controller

00:02:12.091 --> 00:02:14.024 line:85%
on their headset immediately.

00:02:14.024 --> 00:02:17.352 line:91%
<c.yellow>In this case, obviously we are
communicating through handhelds,</c>

00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:19.609 line:91%
<c.yellow>because you are in a simulator
and I'm in a briefing room,</c>

00:02:19.609 --> 00:02:21.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>and this is the only way
we could do it.</c>

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.113 line:91%
Yeah, that's fair enough.
Alright.

00:02:23.113 --> 00:02:25.754 line:85%
We are on autopilot at 15,000 feet.

00:02:26.204 --> 00:02:27.034 line:85%
Let's land this thing.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.969 line:91%
<c.yellow>What I want to try to establish now
is basically where you are,</c>

00:02:32.969 --> 00:02:34.487 line:85%
<c.yellow>and then we're going to discuss</c>

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.504 line:91%
<c.yellow>how we are gonna get you
down on the ground safely.</c>

00:02:36.884 --> 00:02:40.573 line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you could see at the
top of that display,</c>

00:02:40.573 --> 00:02:43.979 line:91%
<c.yellow>there should be a box with
three green values in it.</c>

00:02:43.979 --> 00:02:49.774 line:91%
<c.yellow>Something like N1, hopefully LNAV,
and something else.</c>

00:02:49.774 --> 00:02:53.759 line:91%
<c.yellow>Can you say to me what it says
in those three values at the top?</c>

00:02:53.764 --> 00:02:54.639 line:85%
Yes, I can.

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:58.002 position:84% line:85%
Left is MCP[Mike Charlie Papa] SPD[Sierra Papa Delta].

00:02:58.002 --> 00:03:01.165 line:91%
Middle is LNAV.
Right is ALT HOLD.

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:04.109 line:91%
<c.yellow>Perfect. That means that you're
maintaining the altitude now.</c>

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:09.879 line:91%
<c.yellow>And remember that the autopilot
that you've just confirmed is on</c>

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:13.170 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>is like a third crew member.
That's the way that we pilots view it.</c>

00:03:13.649 --> 00:03:16.319 line:91%
<c.yellow>That crew member is perfectly
capable of flying this aircraft.</c>

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:18.034 line:91%
<c.yellow>So what we're gonna do
from now on is</c>

00:03:18.034 --> 00:03:20.647 line:91%
<c.yellow>we're going to try to tell
that autopilot what to do,</c>

00:03:20.647 --> 00:03:22.589 line:91%
<c.yellow>in order to get you safely
down on the ground, okay?</c>

00:03:23.549 --> 00:03:26.633 line:91%
Understood, and we're aiming for
Dublin Airport, is that right?

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:29.006 align:end position:100% line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah, I have you on radar here,</c>

00:03:29.006 --> 00:03:31.724 align:end position:100% line:91%
<c.yellow>and it looks like you're
pretty close to Dublin Airport.</c>

00:03:31.724 --> 00:03:34.106 align:end size:94% position:94% line:91%
<c.yellow>So that's what
we're going to try to do.</c>

00:03:34.106 --> 00:03:37.846 line:91%
<c.yellow>Now, the top— If you look
below the glare shield,</c>

00:03:37.846 --> 00:03:42.993 align:end position:100% line:91%
<c.yellow>the top panel below the glare shield,
it's called a mode control panel.</c>

00:03:43.604 --> 00:03:48.994 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>It has a lot of windows with numerical
figures in them and a lot of buttons.</c>

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:51.130 line:91%
<c.yellow>Do you know which panel
I'm talking about?</c>

00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:52.904 line:85%
I believe so.

00:03:52.904 --> 00:03:56.374 line:91%
That would be directly below
the windscreen, the windshield.

00:03:57.134 --> 00:04:00.204 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, that's correct.
That panel controls the autopilot.</c>

00:04:00.614 --> 00:04:01.214 line:85%
<c.yellow>Okay?</c>

00:04:01.214 --> 00:04:04.830 line:91%
You will see on the right-hand side
that there is one button

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.331 line:91%
<c.yellow>that says CMD [Charlie Mike Delta],
and it would be green. Confirm.</c>

00:04:09.054 --> 00:04:10.094 line:85%
Confirmed.

00:04:10.094 --> 00:04:11.444 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah, that's the autopilot button.</c>

00:04:11.449 --> 00:04:13.887 line:91%
<c.yellow>Do not press that because that
disconnects the autopilot,</c>

00:04:13.887 --> 00:04:15.194 line:85%
<c.yellow>and that will be a very bad day.</c>

00:04:15.194 --> 00:04:16.995 line:85%
<i>(wheezing)</i>

00:04:16.995 --> 00:04:18.524 line:91%
Understood.
Not touching that button.

00:04:18.907 --> 00:04:20.414 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>(laughs)</i> Okay.</c>

00:04:20.414 --> 00:04:24.400 line:91%
<c.yellow>If you can find the window
that says Altitude on it.</c>

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.684 line:85%
<c.yellow>Tell me when you've seen it.</c>

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.900 line:85%
I see it. It reads 15,000.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.240 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah. Just below that,
there is a knob.</c>

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.606 line:85%
<c.yellow>Can you turn that knob</c>

00:04:31.606 --> 00:04:34.110 line:91%
<c.yellow>until the value reads
4,000 feet instead?</c>

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.400 line:91%
Confirmed.
That now reads 4,000.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.882 line:91%
The wheels next to
what I assume is the throttle

00:04:41.882 --> 00:04:44.134 line:91%
just started spinning
on their own,

00:04:44.134 --> 00:04:46.950 position:58% line:91%
and the plane is now banking
very, very, very heavily to the left.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.683 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, that's because
it's following</c>

00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:51.424 line:91%
<c.yellow>the LNAV track that it has
pre-programmed.</c>

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.427 line:85%
<c.yellow>Don't worry about that.</c>

00:04:52.427 --> 00:04:56.669 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, so the aircraft is now
descending down to 4,000 feet.</c>

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:58.694 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's what we've told it,
and it's now following,</c>

00:04:58.694 --> 00:05:00.719 line:91%
<c.yellow>heading 2-7-0,
so we're good, right.</c>

00:05:00.719 --> 00:05:02.907 line:91%
<c.yellow>The aircraft is doing exactly what
it's supposed to do,</c>

00:05:02.907 --> 00:05:06.325 line:91%
<c.yellow>and what we wanna figure out now is
how much time we have to do this.</c>

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.976 line:91%
<c.yellow>So in the screen that is
second from the left,</c>

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:13.978 line:91%
<c.yellow>in the right hand corner there,
there should be a value of</c>

00:05:13.978 --> 00:05:16.042 line:91%
<c.yellow>how much fuel in total
that you have on board.</c>

00:05:16.042 --> 00:05:17.260 line:85%
<c.yellow>Can you read that out to me?</c>

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.531 line:85%
Yep. Confirm total 3.8.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.785 line:85%
<c.yellow>3.8, okay, that's perfect.</c>

00:05:22.785 --> 00:05:25.755 line:91%
<c.yellow>So that's quite a lot of fuel.
So we have plenty of time.</c>

00:05:25.935 --> 00:05:27.525 line:85%
<c.yellow>Alright. So time is not an issue.</c>

00:05:28.125 --> 00:05:30.945 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>From now on, it's gonna start to be
a little bit more complicated, okay?</c>

00:05:30.945 --> 00:05:32.925 line:91%
<c.yellow>Because now we have the
aircraft on the controls.</c>

00:05:32.925 --> 00:05:34.906 line:91%
<c.yellow>So now we're gonna try
to get it into position</c>

00:05:34.906 --> 00:05:36.225 line:85%
<c.yellow>from which it can auto-land.</c>

00:05:36.225 --> 00:05:39.127 line:91%
<c.yellow>So first of all, I want you
to get your seat adjusted,</c>

00:05:39.127 --> 00:05:42.795 line:91%
<c.yellow>where you can rest your feet
on the pedals easily.</c>

00:05:43.725 --> 00:05:45.658 line:91%
If this is an ejector seat,
I'm gonna kill him!

00:05:48.104 --> 00:05:49.367 line:85%
Yep, okay, I'm in position.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:51.085 line:91%
<c.yellow>Alright, so what we need
to do now is,</c>

00:05:51.085 --> 00:05:52.664 line:85%
<c.yellow>you're going way too fast, okay?</c>

00:05:52.994 --> 00:05:56.054 line:91%
<c.yellow>We need to get your speed back
in order to make a safe landing.</c>

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:59.297 line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you go up to the
mode control panel again,</c>

00:05:59.297 --> 00:06:02.108 line:85%
<c.yellow>and you go out to the left side,</c>

00:06:02.108 --> 00:06:06.075 line:91%
<c.yellow>the second window from the left
should read IAS or Mach.</c>

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.565 line:91%
<c.yellow>Can you tell me again what
the number is in that window?</c>

00:06:09.255 --> 00:06:10.414 line:85%
2-9-1.

00:06:11.039 --> 00:06:14.520 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, that means that you're flying
291 knots at the moment.</c>

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:18.119 line:91%
Can you bring that value
back to 220 knots?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.340 line:85%
2-2-0 confirmed.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:22.600 line:85%
<c.yellow>Perfect.</c>

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.428 align:start size:94% position:6% line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(C major tone)</i></c>

00:06:24.104 --> 00:06:26.309 line:91%
<c.yellow>Can you just tell me if
the speed is reducing?</c>

00:06:27.179 --> 00:06:29.434 line:91%
No, it's not. There was also
just a very loud beep

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:32.189 line:91%
that sounded like a dial tone
for about two seconds.

00:06:32.609 --> 00:06:33.899 line:85%
<c.yellow>You can disregard that for now.</c>

00:06:33.899 --> 00:06:36.899 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's because you are about
to level off at your altitude.</c>

00:06:37.379 --> 00:06:38.556 line:85%
That's good. Okay.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:41.444 line:85%
The speed is not decreasing.

00:06:41.444 --> 00:06:42.884 line:85%
We're still at 262.

00:06:42.884 --> 00:06:44.433 line:85%
<c.yellow>Well, if you're at 262,</c>

00:06:44.433 --> 00:06:46.544 line:91%
<c.yellow>and you were at 293,
then it is reducing.</c>

00:06:46.844 --> 00:06:49.274 line:91%
Oh yeah, I'm just
nearly panicking slightly.

00:06:49.274 --> 00:06:51.074 line:91%
I forgot this was a simulator
for a minute.

00:06:51.074 --> 00:06:51.824 line:85%
Okay, good.

00:06:51.824 --> 00:06:54.254 line:91%
<c.yellow>Now we're gonna turn you,
turn the aircraft again.</c>

00:06:54.254 --> 00:06:56.834 line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you go back up to the
mode control panel</c>

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:58.863 line:91%
<c.yellow>and look at the
heading window again.</c>

00:06:59.804 --> 00:07:01.534 line:85%
Yep. Currently reading 270.

00:07:02.084 --> 00:07:04.835 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, can you turn
that knob below that</c>

00:07:04.835 --> 00:07:08.271 line:91%
<c.yellow>to the left until you get
a number of 100 on it?</c>

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.293 line:85%
100 confirmed.

00:07:11.293 --> 00:07:14.189 line:91%
The plane immediately started
banking heavily to the left.

00:07:14.219 --> 00:07:15.929 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, that's exactly
what we wanted to do.</c>

00:07:15.929 --> 00:07:17.815 line:91%
<c.yellow>'Cause what I'm doing now
is I'm actually</c>

00:07:17.815 --> 00:07:20.309 line:91%
<c.yellow>turning you downwind
for the landing, okay?</c>

00:07:20.669 --> 00:07:23.599 line:91%
I cannot overstate
how unnerving it is

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:27.149 line:91%
to be in a motion-based simulator
for the first time in my life.

00:07:27.149 --> 00:07:29.280 line:85%
It is so convincing!

00:07:30.239 --> 00:07:32.099 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah, no, that's the idea.</c>

00:07:32.549 --> 00:07:36.372 line:91%
<c.yellow>Right, so you are currently
maintaining 4,000 feet,</c>

00:07:36.372 --> 00:07:38.596 line:91%
<c.yellow>and can you tell me what speed
you're keeping at the moment?</c>

00:07:39.689 --> 00:07:41.062 line:85%
2-1-9.

00:07:41.429 --> 00:07:46.349 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>Now you are coming almost perfectly
abeam the airfield now, which is great.</c>

00:07:46.349 --> 00:07:48.871 line:91%
<c.yellow>So the next thing that
I want you to do is,</c>

00:07:48.871 --> 00:07:50.834 line:85%
<c.yellow>to the right of the thrust levers,</c>

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:53.264 line:91%
<c.yellow>there is a flap lever.
Do you see that?</c>

00:07:53.834 --> 00:07:54.569 line:85%
I see it.

00:07:54.764 --> 00:07:58.064 line:91%
<c.yellow>I want you to move that flap lever
to the five position.</c>

00:07:58.184 --> 00:07:59.729 line:85%
<c.yellow>If you have to go through a gate,</c>

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:01.484 line:91%
<c.yellow>first one, and then
you can move it to five.</c>

00:08:03.284 --> 00:08:06.044 line:91%
Yep. That caused the
trim wheels to spin, a lot.

00:08:06.824 --> 00:08:09.730 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, so what's happening
now is that the flaps,</c>

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.481 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>those things at the back of the wings,
they're now extending.</c>

00:08:12.481 --> 00:08:14.942 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's causing a lot of drag
and a lot of shift</c>

00:08:14.942 --> 00:08:18.165 line:91%
<c.yellow>in the way that
the aircraft needs to fly.</c>

00:08:18.165 --> 00:08:20.000 line:85%
<c.yellow>So that's why the trims are moving.</c>

00:08:20.035 --> 00:08:22.905 line:91%
<c.yellow>They're trying to readjust to
this new configuration.</c>

00:08:23.145 --> 00:08:25.275 line:91%
<c.yellow>But this also allows us
to reduce the speed.</c>

00:08:25.455 --> 00:08:27.375 line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you go back up to
the speed selector.</c>

00:08:28.845 --> 00:08:29.345 line:85%
Yep.

00:08:29.835 --> 00:08:33.105 line:85%
<c.yellow>Bring that back to 180 knots.</c>

00:08:35.355 --> 00:08:38.715 line:91%
1-8-0. I can actually feel us
slowing down in here.

00:08:39.765 --> 00:08:41.186 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah. Yep.
That's what we want.</c>

00:08:41.355 --> 00:08:42.216 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's what we want.</c>

00:08:42.675 --> 00:08:45.240 line:91%
<c.yellow>So now we're in a
really good position, okay.</c>

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.978 line:85%
<c.yellow>The flaps are coming out.</c>

00:08:46.978 --> 00:08:49.775 line:85%
<c.yellow>The radials are all set up.</c>

00:08:49.775 --> 00:08:53.400 line:91%
<c.yellow>And basically, I'm just waiting to
turn you in for final now.</c>

